# Test that declaring a CapabilityBase-derived capability statically
# without passing it to .with() causes INSTALL EXTENSION to fail with a
# clear, named diagnostic from the SDK's per-.so capability registry,
# rather than loading an extension whose vtable would be null at call
# time.
#
# This extension's builder has no .with() call, so required_capability_count
# is 0 and the server's "preview capabilities OFF" gate does not fire.
# The SDK-side registry check fires regardless of that setting, since it
# only looks at CapabilityBase-derived statics declared in the .so.

call mtr.add_suppression("vef_register returned an error");
call mtr.add_suppression("was declared but never passed to .with");

--echo # PingCapability was declared but never passed to .with(): INSTALL EXTENSION
--echo # fails at vef_register time with a named diagnostic.
--error ER_VILLAGESQL_GENERIC_ERROR
INSTALL EXTENSION vsql_preview_ping_no_cap_test;
